arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Fix cluster idle and add what system sleep needs

The first patch fixes the CPU cluster idle states, which firmware has been
rejecting by the million: they don't describe states this SoC has. It
stands alone, and has a Fixes tag.

The rest add MPM and a system power domain, as QCM2290 has, and RPM master
stats to see the result with. With these the system power state is entered,
both from idle and in s2idle. The RPM's vlow and vmin counts stay at zero,
so the SoC doesn't reach XO shutdown yet: on this phone the ADSP doesn't go
idle, and until it does this can't be shown to do any good beyond that.

With the system domain's parent being MPM, the PSCI domain probe defers on
each boot, which uncovered two bugs in the genpd core. Without "pmdomain:
core: Wait for a genpd's device links before it can be freed", from another
series, this series exposes memory corruption on each boot. Please take
that one first.

Only tested on a Moto G Power (2021). The RB2 and OnePlus Nord N100 include
this SoC's dtsi as well, and nothing here has been tried on them. Waking
from a TLMM GPIO through MPM hasn't been tried either.
